From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: arm64: dts: h713: drop the AV1 node of 0024 that no driver binds

Two nodes sat at 0x01c0d000: av1-decoder@1c0d000 from 0024 (compatible
"allwinner,sunxi-google-ve", "allwinner,sun50i-h713-av1-decoder", status
"okay", the video engine's resets RST_BUS_VE and RST_BUS_VE3, no driver)
and av1@1c0d000 from 0302, the node hantro's H713 variant binds and 0310
disables. dtc warns about the duplicate unit address (W=1,
unique_unit_address). A driver written for either string of the first,
or the AV1 decoder brought back, would meet a second, enabled node that
names the video engine's resets.

The first node goes. decd_reserved stays: the TV decoder (dec@5600000)
uses it.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi | 15 ---------------
 1 file changed, 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
index 0af693952..60ee4c271 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -1353,21 +1353,6 @@ iommu: iommu@2010000 {
 		 * Testing without SRAM property first - may be optional on H713.
 		 */
 
-		/*
-		 * H713 AV1 decoder block (separate address from Cedrus VE to avoid 0x01c0e000 conflict)
-		 */
-		av1_decoder: av1-decoder@1c0d000 {
-			compatible = "allwinner,sunxi-google-ve", "allwinner,sun50i-h713-av1-decoder";
-			reg = <0x01c0d000 0x1000>, <0x03000000 0x10>;
-			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 107 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
-			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_VE>, <&ccu CLK_BUS_VE3>, <&ccu CLK_BUS_AV1>, <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VE3>;
-			clock-names = "bus_ve", "bus_ve3", "av1", "mbus_ve3";
-			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_VE>, <&ccu RST_BUS_VE3>;
-			reset-names = "reset_ve", "reset_ve3";
-			memory-region = <&decd_reserved>;
-			status = "okay";
-		};
-
 		ve: video-codec@1c0e000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h6-video-engine";
 			/*
